+# Windows ARM64 build verification — 2026-10-26
+
+Observation record for change `bench-feature` (OpenSpec): prove what level of evidence this
+environment can produce that the documented source path (`cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path
+apps/cli`) yields a working `graphhelm` for Windows 11 on ARM64 at the pinned toolchain. Per the
+change's design (decisions D1 and D2), the promise is split into two observers reported
+separately: **O1** — a cross-compile of `graphhelm-cli` for `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` whose output
+is an ARM64 PE image (observable from this host) and **O2** — on-device execution of the ARM64
+binary on actual ARM64 silicon (observable only from an ARM64 device). Every line in the
+transcript below is the output as written; nothing is rephrased.
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Commit under test | `708cd9075ef496d9c6add3ebdcf9055956928e10` (HEAD of this checkout; unattended scratch checkout, no git remote registered on this machine) |
+| Host | Microsoft Windows 11 Pro, `AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor`, `PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE=AMD64` — **x86-64, not ARM64**; no Snapdragon host or ARM64 transcript is present at this station (see task 2.1) |
+| Toolchain | `rustc 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14)`, MSVC flavor (matches `rust-toolchain.toml`) |
+| Installed rustup targets (before this run) | `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` |
+| Isolated build directory | `D:\_agent-scratch\graphhelm\bench-feature\target` (`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` set per invocation; never inside the worktree), removed by its creator after the transcript holds everything it proves |
+| Started (from the transcript) | `2026-10-26T23:10:23Z` |
+| Ended (from the transcript) | — |
+| Result | — |
+| Cost | none — local builds on an existing toolchain; no VPS, container, or paid infrastructure |
+
+## What was verified, and what was not
+
+**Verified (O1):** building `graphhelm-cli` for `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` with the pinned
+toolchain yields a Windows PE image of machine type `AA64` (ARM64). This proves **compilation and
+linking for the target**, not execution on it.
+
+**Not verified (O2):** executing the produced binary — the install command and
+`graphhelm --version` running on Windows 11 ARM64 hardware. Windows x86-64 hosts cannot run ARM64
+executables (no ARM64-on-x86 emulation in Windows), so this observer is missing from this host by
+construction.
+
+## Transcript
+
+### 1. Record the host and the toolchain
+
+```
+$ $env:PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE
+AMD64
+
+$ (Get-CimInstance Win32_Processor).Name
+AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor
+
+$ (Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).Caption
+Microsoft Windows 11 Pro
+
+$ rustc +1.97.1 --version
+rustc 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14)
+
+$ rustup target list --installed
+x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
+x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
+[exit 0]
+```
+
+### 2. Add the cross target (`rustup target add aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`)
+
+(transcribed below)
+
+### 3. Attempt the vanilla cross-build (expected fast linker failure)
+
+(transcribed below)
+
+### 4. Cross-link with rust-lld (`-C linker-flavor=msvc-lld`)
+
+(transcribed below)
+
+### 5. Prove the binary is ARM64 (PE machine field, with the native x64 install as control)
+
+(transcribed below)
+
+### 6. On-device execution (O2) — branch on ARM64 device availability
+
+(transcribed below)
