+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Windows 11 on ARM64 (Snapdragon) laptops are common developer machines, but the getting-started
+page currently verifies the CLI only for the prebuilt x86-64 archives ("verified Windows and
+Ubuntu x86-64 archives", section 1) and sends every ARM host to an unproven build-from-source
+path (`docs/releases/0.1.0.md`: "For macOS, ARM, and other hosts, build from source"). An ARM64
+user today has no documented, verified way to get a working `graphhelm`. This change proves the
+documented install path works for Windows ARM64 at the pinned toolchain and records Windows ARM64
+as a verified platform in `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`, scoped precisely to what was observed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Verification (no code changes): establish that the `graphhelm` CLI installs on Windows 11 ARM64
+  via the documented source path (`cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path apps/cli`) and runs
+  `graphhelm --version`, using the strongest observer available on the build host and an ARM64
+  host where available (see design for the split, since the planning host is x86-64).
+- Documentation: `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` section 1 lists **Windows ARM64** among the
+  verified platforms, replacing the blanket "build from source" routing for ARM with the verified
+  statement plus the exact commands and their expected `graphhelm 0.1.0` output.
+- Evidence: the observation record (commands, outputs, host facts) is kept where acceptance
+  transcripts already live (`docs/acceptance/`), because this page's claims are anchored to such
+  transcripts.
+- Explicitly out of scope: publishing a prebuilt ARM64 release archive, changes to
+  `docs/releases/0.1.0.md`, CI/release pipeline work, and any code or dependency changes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `cli-installation`: How users obtain and first run the `graphhelm` binary — the supported
+  install paths (prebuilt release archives vs. build from source) and which host platforms each
+  path is verified for, including Windows ARM64.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(none — `openspec/specs/` contains no existing capability specs)
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected documentation: `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` (section 1, "Build or install the
+  binary"); one acceptance transcript under `docs/acceptance/` recording the observation.
+- No Rust code, schema, wire format, dependency, or toolchain changes. The pinned toolchain stays
+  `1.97.1`; verification only adds the `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` target to the verifying machine,
+  which is environment state, not a repository change.
+- Compatibility: none — documentation and evidence only; no behavior changes for existing
+  platforms.
