+# Tasks
+
+Reference: specs in `specs/cli-installation/spec.md`, approach in `design.md` (decisions D1–D4).
+No Rust code changes in any task. If a step in section 1 cannot run (network, toolchain), stop and
+report the change blocked with the verbatim error before writing anything under section 3.
+
+## 1. Evidence: cross-compile the CLI for Windows ARM64 (observer O1)
+
+- [x] 1.1 Start the acceptance transcript skeleton
+  `docs/acceptance/windows-arm64-verify-2026-10-26.md` in the house format (metadata table with
+  commit under test = checkout HEAD, host facts, started timestamp, cost: none), recording the
+  measured host facts (`PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE`, CPU model, OS caption, `rustc +1.97.1 --version`,
+  installed rustup targets). Verify: file exists with the metadata table populated and the host
+  identified as non-ARM64.
+- [ ] 1.2 Add the cross target: `rustup target add aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`. Verify:
+  `rustup target list --installed` now lists `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`; record the download result
+  in the transcript. On network failure, stop per the section preamble.
+- [ ] 1.3 Attempt the vanilla cross-build
+  `cargo +1.97.1 build --locked -p graphhelm-cli --target aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` into an isolated
+  `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` under the approved lane scratch root (not the worktree). Expected: a fast
+  linker-not-found failure (ARM64 MSVC linker absent, measured at planning). Verify: the verbatim
+  failure is captured in the transcript and is a toolchain/linker error, not a compile error in
+  GraphHelm sources.
+- [ ] 1.4 Cross-link with rust-lld (design D2.3): rerun 1.3 with
+  `$env:RUSTFLAGS = "-C linker-flavor=msvc-lld"` against the same isolated target dir. Verify: exit
+  code 0 and `target/aarch64-pc-windows-msvc/debug/graphhelm.exe` exists; capture the tail of the
+  build output (`Finished …` line) in the transcript.
+- [ ] 1.5 (conditional — only if 1.4 fails) Install the VS Build Tools 2022 ARM64 C++ workload via
+  winget and rerun 1.3 verbatim. Verify: build green, or the change is reported blocked with both
+  failures captured verbatim.
+- [ ] 1.6 Prove the binary is ARM64: read the PE machine field of the produced `graphhelm.exe`
+  (and of the existing `%USERPROFILE%\.cargo\bin\graphhelm.exe` as a control). Verify: the built
+  binary reads `0xAA64` and the control reads `0x8664`; both values recorded in the transcript.
+- [ ] 1.7 Clean up the isolated target directory by name (creator removes its own), after the
+  transcript holds everything it proves. Verify: directory gone, `git status` shows no stray files
+  inside the checkout.
+
+## 2. On-device execution (observer O2) — branch on device availability
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Determine whether an ARM64 Windows device (or a captured transcript from one) is
+  reachable from this environment. **If yes:** on that device run the documented §1 path natively
+  (`cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path apps/cli`, then `graphhelm --version`) and append the
+  transcript, asserting output `graphhelm 0.1.0` and exit code 0. **If no:** append exactly
+  `OBSERVER_MISSING: on-device execution of the ARM64 binary on Windows 11 ARM64 hardware` to the
+  transcript's "not verified" section. Verify: the transcript ends with exactly one of the two
+  outcomes, stated verbatim.
+
+## 3. Documentation — word the claim at exactly the proven level
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Finish the transcript (sections "verified vs. not verified", proof-level classification
+  per design D1, ended timestamp, result line classifying pass/OBSERVER_MISSING parts separately).
+  Verify: metadata table complete; every command in the "verified" section has its verbatim output
+  beside it; the OBSERVER_MISSING line (if applicable) is present word for word.
+- [ ] 3.2 Edit `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` section 1 only: add Windows ARM64 to the
+  verified-platforms statement, naming the verified path (build from source at pinned toolchain),
+  citing the new transcript, and stating the proof level the transcript actually holds; adjust the
+  closing "On macOS or another platform, build from source" sentence so ARM hosts are no longer
+  lumped with unproven platforms while macOS remains build-from-source-only. Verify: the diff
+  touches no other section; every "verified" adjective in the new sentence has a matching transcript
+  line; the relative link to the transcript resolves.
+- [ ] 3.3 Evidence-to-wording audit: re-read the final §1 text against the final transcript.
+  Verify (checklist recorded in the PR body): no claim exceeds the transcript; macOS and other
+  platforms are still presented as build-from-source, not verified; expected-banner text matches
+  design D4 (`graphhelm 0.1.0`).
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once the project's review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result (`openspec show cli-installation --type spec` lists both requirements).
